      {
        "n": "GUITAR WORLD: A GUIDE TO SHIBUYA-KEI (R)",
        "s": "2026-11-08T17:00:00Z",
        "e": "2026-11-08T18:00:00Z",
        "d": "Translating literally as “Shibuya-style”, named after the shopping district of Tokyo, which during the ‘90s was the epicentre of the kitsch and Western retro throwback aesthetic, Shibuya-kei bands drew heavily from easy listening pop movements of the 1960s – bossa nova, psychedelia, yé-yé and more.",
        "j": "A GUIDE TO SHIBUYA-KEI",
        "u": "https://www.nts.live/api/v2/shows/guitar-world/episodes/a-guide-to-shibuya-kei-1st-august-2022",
        "t": "restream"
      },
      {
        "n": "IN FOCUS: POISON GIRL FRIEND (R)",
        "s": "2026-11-08T18:00:00Z",
        "e": "2026-11-08T19:00:00Z",
        "d": "Born in Tokyo, raised in Brazil, and educated in French schools, but it was in London that Noriko Sekiguchi, also known as POiSON GiRL FRiEND first found the music that would inspire her own work. She became infatuated with the UK and US house music that was filling the city in the mid to late 1980s, before returning to Tokyo, bringing the music with her to the city's clubs as a DJ. \nReleasing multiple albums, the POiSON GiRLFRiEND project – featuring a house and breakbeat-infused pop and R&B sound – reached minor commercial and critical acclaim. Sekiguchi's solo music along with her work in obscure group Kiss-O-Matic has experienced a small revival following some Japanese music fanatics exploration of 90s CD releases. ",
        "j": "POISON GIRL FRIEND",
        "u": "https://www.nts.live/api/v2/shows/in-focus/episodes/poison-girlfriend-9th-september-2022",
        "t": "restream"
      },
